# Keeps `docker build`'s context small and secret-free. None of these are
# COPYed into any image (each Dockerfile copies only the specific
# directories it needs), but without this file the daemon still has to
# read and transmit all of them as part of the build context on every
# build — confirmed: 1.79GB sent (mostly .venv/ + mlruns/ + data/) with
# this file absent, vs. a few MB of actual source for what gets copied.
.venv/
.venv-loadtest/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

.git/
.github/

data/
artifacts/
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
predictors/
reports/
logs/
*.log
*.db

.env
*.token

docs/
tests/
schedule/
databricks/
.backup-prior-run/
README.md

# NOTE: assets/ is deliberately NOT ignored — Dockerfile.serve and
# Dockerfile.train COPY the name index from it (see tests/unit/test_deployment_config.py).
